  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures Mountain Goats performing at Lee's Palace in Toronto on October 17, 2005 [1]. Taped by Peter Sohriakoff, the file contains eighteen songs and runs for sixty-seven minutes [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific show in the archive [1]. The setlist begins with Broom People and Linda Blair Was Born Innocent, followed by Color in Your Cheeks and Nine Black Poppies [1]. The group then plays Love Love Love, Tollund Man, and Game Shows Touch Our Lives [1]. First Few Desperate Hours and Dinu Lipatti's Bones continue the sequence, leading into Twin Human Highway Flares [1]. A brief tuning segment precedes Song for Dennis Brown and Dance Music [1]. The main set concludes with Lion's Teeth, Oceanographer's Choice, and Against Pollution [1]. After an encore break, the band performs See America Right, Palmcorder Yajna, and California Song [1]. The uploader notes that the first few minutes of Twin Human Highway Flares are missing because the recorder was dropped on the floor [1]. There is significant microphone noise at the end of that song [1]. Oceanographer's Choice and Against Pollution are noted as being performed with Prayers & Tears of Arthur Digby Sellers [1]. The beginning of the final song, California Song, also contains microphone noise [1].",
